=> if IN WINDOW is empty for all c, the AP-completion step holds: adding a 12th runner
   to a dilated AP-11 gives tight (complete the AP) or loose (M>=2/25), never in-window.
   This is the inductive core of (C)/hdich given the 11-subfamily-tight hypothesis.
